\begin_layout Section
Contribution
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this thesis, the principle of familiarity is introduced, by means of
 which solutions are characterized as interpretable the less they deviate
 from the expert's solution program.
 To our knowledge, familiarity is a novel technique in the domain of explainable
 AI, which has not yet been used as a reference for better understanding
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "fehrer_hein_tokic_udluft_2020"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This is achieved by replacing the absolute node-count metric in genetic
 programming with the tree edit distance; a measure which is calculated
 as the number of edits to an expert's programming tree.
 To further enhance familiarity in the solutions, techniques such as defining
 a fixed core structure or tree unification are implemented.
 The evaluation will be discussed regarding the success of preserving structures
 and the opportunity of familiarity, as well as the implications on offline
 and online performance or security.
 
\end_layout

