Reinforcement Learning
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Reinforcement-learning"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Reinforcement learning is a subfield of machine learning, where an agent
 has to derive a policy through interaction with an environment in order
 to maximize the sum of future reward.
 Problems include games or simulations, where a goal is predefined, but
 a solution strategy must be sought.
 The environment is formalized as Markov Decision Process (MDP) as can be
 seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:RL-basics"

\end_inset

, which is a stochastic form of determinism [xxx] so that in each state,
 when performing an action, the same subsequent state is reached with a
 certain probability.
 The policy can be learned as mapping between states and actions, which
 is an implicit representation, or as explicitly defined rule set, but regardles
s of that, learning through interaction requires carefully weighting up
 exploration of new states and actions and exploitation of the learned policy.
 
\end_layout

