\begin_layout Subsection
Offline Fitness Function: Symbolic Regression 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "Symbolic-Regression"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The fitness function is required to compare candidates.
 A symbolic regression is a common offline implementation to calculate how
 well a formula can explain data.
 The regression error must become as small as possible, which is the sum
 of the distance between the outputs and predicted values of a data set.
 Both the mean average error (MAE) and the mean square error (MSE) are regressio
n metrics (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:regression-error"
caps "true"

\end_inset

).
 The MAE indicates the average deviation from the target solution and is
 distance-true.
 The MSE, however, severely punishes outliers, lumps of strong deviation
 and volatile solutions, which can lead to a better overall generalization.
\end_layout

