\begin_layout Standard
For this work, a GP suite in the language Python was developed.
 The evaluation process is accelerated with Tensorflow enabled evaluation,
 inspired by Karoo 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "karooGPpaper"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, but required a complete restructuring.
 The more detailed implementation is described below.
 Fitness evaluation is the bottleneck of performance.
 Kai Staats has shown with Karoo that a 2-15 times speedup can be achieved
 by converting expressions into Tensorflow graphs, which enables parallel
 evaluation on the GPU.
 To further enable simplification of expressions, the Python library SymPy
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "10.7717/peerj-cs.103"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 was extended, which uses symbolic mathematics and thus sifts out unnecessary
 calculations before evaluation.
 The memory usage and performance could be further increased, largely thanks
 to the help of lookup-tables for tree evaluation, passing variables locally
 and especially using recursive tree structures.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The runtime reduced to about 50% and memory usage to 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$
\backslash
approx 10
\backslash
%$
\end_layout

\end_inset

