\begin_layout Paragraph
Black Box: SARSA neuropolicy
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The OpenAI-Gym implementation features a leaderboard
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "https://github.com/openai/gym/wiki/Leaderboard"
target "https://github.com/openai/gym/wiki/Leaderboard"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\end_inset

 that contains the fastest learning approach for each problem, from which
 we have selected the top ranked neuropolicy.
 Unfortunately, the leaderboard only includes the fastest learning approaches,
 not the best performing.
 At the time, the top ranked was a SARSA approach with tiling that required
 75 training episodes to find a sufficient model, with an average reward
 of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$-103.41$
\end_layout

\end_inset

 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "xiao2019"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
At this state, the agent outperforms the vanilla-expert solution, but it
 is still a very inexperienced, e.g.
 it reverses just before the target for no reason as can be seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "sarsa75_problem_decision_plots"

\end_inset

.
 In rare cases, this leads to outlier episodes (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:ml-sarsa-outliers"

\end_inset

).
 Since such problems could not be noticed in reality, the approach was evaluated
, especially in safety-critical areas, more attention would be paid to safety.
 For comparison, the results were also evaluated with a more 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

experienced
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 version that trained for 200 episodes, in which the previously mentioned
 uncertainties play a much smaller role (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "sarsa-200-plots"

\end_inset

).
 The performance increases accordingly by almost 5 steps to 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$
\backslash
approx-98.7$
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 Further training did not lead to further improvements; on the contrary,
 the models deteriorated strongly (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "sarsa1000-plots"

\end_inset

), what might be caused to the non-convergence of SARSA approaches.
\end_layout

