\begin_layout Subsection
Mountain car Discussion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
All origin programs could be improved with familiar approaches and showed
 significant structural difference to regular GP candidates.
 Simple expert heuristics have shown limitations regarding the tree edit
 distance, but can be solved by defining a fixed core.
 The more experienced SARSA-200 policy was easier to fit than SARSA-75.
 Methods of restricting the search space, such as fixed nodes or a reduced
 operator set have shown better online performance, which also encourages
 the claim that simple and structured mathematics deliver the better results.
 The extraordinary performance can probably be explained by the optimised
 search space, which could be reduced to an efficient and smaller space
 by the expert's specification.
 
\end_layout

