\begin_layout Plain Layout
A very simple mathematical formula can be much harder to understand than
 a comprehensive strategy that is intuitive; the solutions achieve almost
 identical results.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

The if-conditional exemplifies the contradiction between interpretability
 and a count-based measure.
 Although the if-operator has the highest arity with 3 input parameters,
 it creates more structure than other operators, as its child trees are
 separated chunks, often even reoccurring chunks if patterns are matched.
 Due to the high branching factor, this operator should not be further weighted.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "fig:if-operator-composition"

\end_inset


\end_layout

