\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The blue path is the familiar and trusted way up the hill, the green path
 is a faster solution.
 Starting from the origin path, there are several path candidates.
 A regular regression only evaluates the deviation from the target solution;
 path (1.) and path (2.) would be equally good.
 However, path (1.) achieves this with a much smaller change in behavior,
 which is preferable from a trust perspective.
 In contrast, path (3.) is even worse than the known solution.
 Lastly, path (4.) deviates early and affects the succeeding strategy.
 
